WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.437
The federal requirement.

2
00:00:01.437 --> 00:00:06.409
Every control the checks evidence is in
the NIST special publication eight hundred

3
00:00:06.409 --> 00:00:10.244
fifty-three, revision five, Moderate
baseline: system monitoring,

4
00:00:10.244 --> 00:00:14.718
malicious code protection and audit
record generation, through the agents;

5
00:00:14.718 --> 00:00:17.488
boundary protection,
through the network path;

6
00:00:17.488 --> 00:00:22.175
unsupported system components and flaw
remediation; the component inventory;

7
00:00:22.175 --> 00:00:25.513
and continuous monitoring
and configuration settings.

8
00:00:25.513 --> 00:00:29.700
The mapping is the program's reading;
the agency's assessor decides.

9
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:33.290
The evidence an ISSO keeps:
each check's dated output,

10
00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:36.462
with its evidences list
and machines in scope;

11
00:00:36.462 --> 00:00:39.634
the app's Reader role
assignment and its scope;

12
00:00:39.634 --> 00:00:43.558
a decision for each unsupported
server, migrate, upgrade,

13
00:00:43.558 --> 00:00:45.645
or isolate and accept the risk;

14
00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:51.071
the E S U subscription record for each
instance whose coverage isn't confirmed;

15
00:00:51.071 --> 00:00:56.497
the dated decision behind each do-not-enforce
assignment; and for each Windows

16
00:00:56.497 --> 00:01:00.838
Server 2016 server still in
production after January twelfth,

17
00:01:00.838 --> 00:01:02.675
2027, the exception record.

18
00:01:02.675 --> 00:01:06.940
The Arc track implementation guide's
Step 8 puts this on a schedule.
